The attached image is a Western blot (Figure 7D) demonstrating the induction and cleavage of IL-1β in bone marrow-derived dendritic cells. It shows that inactive pro-IL-1β, a 30kD protein, is present in cell lysates, particularly when cells are primed with LPS. Crucially, the presence of a 15kD band, representing the active, cleaved form of IL-1β, is observed in the supernatant predominantly when cells are treated with both LPS and Nano-11. This indicates that Nano-11, in conjunction with LPS priming, effectively promotes the processing and secretion of active IL-1β, a potent pro-inflammatory cytokine essential for dendritic cell activation and immune response enhancement.